virglrenderer: Venus takes values Vulkan ignores, refuses blend states the drivers read past

What: four changes in what vkr counts as read (#624).
- A texel buffer view of the whole size with less than one texel after its offset is legal
  (VUID-VkBufferViewCreateInfo-offset-00925, -range-04059; -range-00928/00929 only apply to
  a range that is not VK_WHOLE_SIZE). vkr refused it. Now, when the guest turned
  nullDescriptor on, vkr makes the view without a driver view: its handle is VK_NULL_HANDLE,
  so every descriptor the guest writes, pushes or copies with it is a null descriptor
  (VUID-VkWriteDescriptorSet-descriptorType-02994/02995), which reads 0, as a view of no
  texel does. The format, usage, offset and alignment checks run first, as before. Its
  destroy frees it without vkr_buffer_view_from_handle (which asserts a driver handle); the
  device's teardown destroys VK_NULL_HANDLE for it, which the drivers skip. Without
  nullDescriptor the view stays refused, with the reason in the line.
- A pipeline's vertex binding stride is not checked against maxVertexInputBindingStride
  while VK_DYNAMIC_STATE_VERTEX_INPUT_BINDING_STRIDE is set: Vulkan ignores it then
  (VUID-VkVertexInputBindingDescription-stride-00619 does not apply; the Khronos layer skips
  it, sl_pipeline.cpp:1188). The stride used is vkCmdBindVertexBuffers2's, which vkr
  already bounds (VUID-vkCmdBindVertexBuffers2-pStrides-03362).
- A color blend state must have its attachment array (attachmentCount > 0) and a count equal
  to the subpass's or rendering's colors wherever Vulkan reads them: not with rasterization
  statically off, not for a library without fragment output, not without colors (vkr let
  those through before and still does). The array is ignored only with the four blend states
  COLOR_BLEND_ENABLE, EQUATION, WRITE_MASK and ADVANCED dynamic
  (VUID-VkPipelineColorBlendStateCreateInfo-pAttachments-07353), the count with the first
  three, and ADVANCED too when advancedBlendCoherentOperations is on
  (VUID-VkGraphicsPipelineCreateInfo-renderPass-07609, -06055); each counts only when the
  guest turned its extendedDynamicState3 feature on (-07378, -07379, -07380, -07386), read
  from the device create chain as vkr reads robustness2.
- Refused buffer ranges in vkCmd* lines say "the whole size" and "no buffer" instead of
  18446744073709551615 and "of 0" (barriers, vertex and index binds v1 and v2, update, fill,
  transform feedback binds, a NULL buffer descriptor). The text is made only on a refusal.
Why: vkr checked the blend state's array and count only when the three dynamic blend states
were set, with or without their features, and let a NULL array through always. Neither Mac
driver has those features. On the M1 Max, straight to the driver (3 runs in 5 modes:
KosmicKrisp, MoltenVK, MoltenVK prefill, each under libgmalloc): a NULL array with nothing
dynamic SIGSEGV on both (Mesa's vk_color_blend_state_init reads pAttachments[a],
vk_graphics_state.c:1047; MoltenVK's addFragmentOutputToPipeline, MVKPipeline.mm:1952), a
NULL array or a count of 9 with the three dynamic SIGSEGV on MoltenVK. With rasterization off
(static) or a subpass without colors a NULL array works on both (15/15 each). The 0-element
view ends the process on both drivers in Metal ("MTLTextureDescriptor has width of zero":
KosmicKrisp at the create, MoltenVK at the descriptor write), so it never goes to them; a
null texel view written, pushed or copied works on KosmicKrisp (6/6 each). A dynamic stride
past the limit works on both, also bound with vkCmdBindVertexBuffers (no strides) and a draw
recorded (15/15, KosmicKrisp 6/6 at 65552).
Left alone: attachmentCount stays <= maxColorAttachments even with the blend states dynamic
(those need the features, and a count of 9 crashes MoltenVK and overflows Mesa's 8-entry
array); MoltenVK has no nullDescriptor (it refuses a device asking for it), so a 0-element
view stays refused there; "of 0" in copy, query and image-copy lines (those sizes cannot be
VK_WHOLE_SIZE). The features are read from the first struct of their type, as robustness2
(see virgl-venus-chain-repeats.patch: Mesa ORs repeats, MoltenVK refuses features it lacks).
Upstream: OmacVM policy (ADR 0065).
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-venus-commands.c (d-texel-*, p-gfx-vstride-dynamic*, p-gfx-blend-*
of case_ignored, c-null-text-*; five also under libgmalloc), test-venus-image-limits.c
(tview-empty).

